(1042582, 124995, 7778, '<td valign="top">This is the 157th image I viewed in this challenge. It is the first one, which caused me to spend a while looking, pondering, thinking, considering...<br/> <br/>how a thing so apparently plain can stir things up. The photo, IMO, is an amusing and delightful commotion. The prospects of finding the undepicted seventh side of the wall within the visual confines of the picture are challenging indeed. Since there is little else in the way of an obvious subject to be had from it, the stimulus is real and effective.<br/> <br/>The artless manner of the photograph and the lack of discernible evidence of post-processing is stark when compared to the considerable complexities posed by composing it. While the choice to centre the corner has resulted in an effective dynamic, the tonal balance over the full dimension of the picture, IMO, could be -and, for a photo which comes with such high demands, should be- better. <br/> <br/>Since darker areas weigh more heavily within a composition, the lighter areas could be more expansive, which inevitably would make for an assymmetric composition. An assymetric composition, however, would also likely accrue the potential for a more abstracted order. This, to my sense of it, would be beneficial for the conceptual appreciation I derived from it.<br/> <br/>I value this photograph for the uniqueness of the genre it represents and for the noetic adventure it invites.  &gt; 7</td>', 'This is the 157th image I viewed in this challenge. It is the first one, which caused me to spend a while looking, pondering, thinking, considering... how a thing so apparently plain can stir things up. The photo, IMO, is an amusing and delightful commotion. The prospects of finding the undepicted seventh side of the wall within the visual confines of the picture are challenging indeed. Since there is little else in the way of an obvious subject to be had from it, the stimulus is real and effective. The artless manner of the photograph and the lack of discernible evidence of post-processing is stark when compared to the considerable complexities posed by composing it. While the choice to centre the corner has resulted in an effective dynamic, the tonal balance over the full dimension of the picture, IMO, could be -and, for a photo which comes with such high demands, should be- better.  Since darker areas weigh more heavily within a composition, the lighter areas could be more expansive, which inevitably would make for an assymmetric composition. An assymetric composition, however, would also likely accrue the potential for a more abstracted order. This, to my sense of it, would be beneficial for the conceptual appreciation I derived from it. I value this photograph for the uniqueness of the genre it represents and for the noetic adventure it invites.  > 7', '2004-12-01 23:32:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1042583, 123839, 25464, '<td valign="top">It has been done before, and it will be done again.  This one is interesting.  I really like the color.  Focus is great. 8.</td>', 'It has been done before, and it will be done again.  This one is interesting.  I really like the color.  Focus is great. 8.', '2004-12-01 23:33:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(1042584, 123608, 18197, '<td valign="top">Maybe we have become jaded by real looking sky and expect heida-like clouds and drama. But for me, if the sky were a bit better defined and possibly with higher contrast, I would give this shot a point or two more.</td>', 'Maybe we have become jaded by real looking sky and expect heida-like clouds and drama. But for me, if the sky were a bit better defined and possibly with higher contrast, I would give this shot a point or two more.', '2004-12-01 23:33:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(1042585, 124754, 27847, '<td valign="top">Nice idea, something to do with the Lord of the Rings? From the light and/or flash it almost looks like that top left and bottom middle rings are silver but that could just be an illusion. The biggest thing here is it looks like the focus was on the letters and not on the rings because they seem a little soft/out of focus.</td>', 'Nice idea, something to do with the Lord of the Rings? From the light and/or flash it almost looks like that top left and bottom middle rings are silver but that could just be an illusion. The biggest thing here is it looks like the focus was on the letters and not on the rings because they seem a little soft/out of focus.', '2004-12-01 23:33:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(1042586, 124822, 28771, '<td valign="top">Good title, good comp. Seven orange slices to spell out six. Clever. Border is a bit much, but not bad. Good texture on the fruit, nice choice of background. You did good pal. (8)</td>', 'Good title, good comp. Seven orange slices to spell out six. Clever. Border is a bit much, but not bad. Good texture on the fruit, nice choice of background. You did good pal. (8)', '2004-12-01 23:34:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(1042587, 125095, 25464, '<td valign="top">Sharp!  (Pun intended).   It doesn''t wow me, but it is a good shot that meets the challenge. 7.</td>', 'Sharp!  (Pun intended).   It doesn''t wow me, but it is a good shot that meets the challenge. 7.', '2004-12-01 23:34:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1042588, 125208, 18197, '<td valign="top">Very nice composition. I like the shadows very much. Hanging on the wall like that, the coats have a "ski-lodge" sort of feel. Warm and cozy. Brings back a lot of fond memories. Great shot. Hope it does well.</td>', 'Very nice composition. I like the shadows very much. Hanging on the wall like that, the coats have a "ski-lodge" sort of feel. Warm and cozy. Brings back a lot of fond memories. Great shot. Hope it does well.', '2004-12-01 23:34:28.000000', NULL, 1),
