(1051586, 124339, 29611, '<td valign="top">well, my first pic over 5, so thats good news. I''ll just keep workin with what i got and i''ve had a blast so far:)</td>', 'well, my first pic over 5, so thats good news. I''ll just keep workin with what i got and i''ve had a blast so far:)', '2004-12-08 03:46:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(1051591, 125077, 15497, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.photo.net/photodb/photo?photo_id=2495564" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">I saw it here.</a></td>', 'I saw it here.', '2004-12-08 04:06:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(1051611, 124465, 9292, '<td valign="top">Thank you all for comments. I´m very happy with my first ribbon. I´m sorry because I don´t have a shot of my original set up, but I´m going to try to explain. It´s easy but I´m a bit perfectionist and  it took me near three hours to achieve the final shot.<br/>First of all I printed a sheet with the title of the challenge. this was done using Powerpoint (for example) and then printed reversed (with the aid of a postscript printer driver)<br/><a href="//img33.exs.cx/img33/2364/background14cu.jpg" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Text<img alt="'' . substr(''//img33.exs.cx/img33/2364/background14cu.th.jpg'', strrpos(''//img33.exs.cx/img33/2364/background14cu.th.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//img33.exs.cx/img33/2364/background14cu.th.jpg"/></a> <br/>This printed text was folded and glued carefully to achieve a perfect transition in the words<br/><a href="//img23.exs.cx/img23/1458/img125226kq.jpg" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Cylinder<img alt="'' . substr(''//img23.exs.cx/img23/1458/img125226kq.th.jpg'', strrpos(''//img23.exs.cx/img23/1458/img125226kq.th.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//img23.exs.cx/img23/1458/img125226kq.th.jpg"/></a> <br/>Still we have a problem beacuse if we take a photo with this setup and look at the center of the balls we can see the body of the rebel<br/><a href="//img7.exs.cx/img7/9844/background20bv.jpg" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">close-up<img alt="'' . substr(''//img7.exs.cx/img7/9844/background20bv.th.jpg'', strrpos(''//img7.exs.cx/img7/9844/background20bv.th.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//img7.exs.cx/img7/9844/background20bv.th.jpg"/></a> <br/>These are the kind of details that scores down our shots in this site. to fix this we can use this close-up to create a mask for our lens and put it at the top of the cylinder<br/><a href="//img7.exs.cx/img7/8563/background39js.jpg" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"> <img alt="'' . substr(''//img7.exs.cx/img7/8563/background39js.th.jpg'', strrpos(''//img7.exs.cx/img7/8563/background39js.th.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//img7.exs.cx/img7/8563/background39js.th.jpg"/></a><a href="//img23.exs.cx/img23/2007/img125236nu.jpg" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"> <img alt="'' . substr(''//img23.exs.cx/img23/2007/img125236nu.th.jpg'', strrpos(''//img23.exs.cx/img23/2007/img125236nu.th.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//img23.exs.cx/img23/2007/img125236nu.th.jpg"/></a><a href="//img130.exs.cx/img130/5528/img12534gr.jpg" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"> <img alt="'' . substr(''//img130.exs.cx/img130/5528/img12534gr.th.jpg'', strrpos(''//img130.exs.cx/img130/5528/img12534gr.th.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//img130.exs.cx/img130/5528/img12534gr.th.jpg"/></a> <br/>With this trick we can hide our camera "completely".<br/>This is a shot without backlighting<br/><a href="//img7.exs.cx/img7/7228/alternate2yv.jpg" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//img7.exs.cx/img7/7228/alternate2yv.th.jpg'', strrpos(''//img7.exs.cx/img7/7228/alternate2yv.th.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//img7.exs.cx/img7/7228/alternate2yv.th.jpg"/></a> <br/>And this is the final shot with backlighting (the setup over a glass table) and without processing.<br/><a href="//img33.exs.cx/img33/5803/original1gh.jpg" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//img33.exs.cx/img33/5803/original1gh.th.jpg'', strrpos(''//img33.exs.cx/img33/5803/original1gh.th.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//img33.exs.cx/img33/5803/original1gh.th.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/></td>', 'Thank you all for comments. I´m very happy with my first ribbon. I´m sorry because I don´t have a shot of my original set up, but I´m going to try to explain. It´s easy but I´m a bit perfectionist and  it took me near three hours to achieve the final shot.First of all I printed a sheet with the title of the challenge. this was done using Powerpoint (for example) and then printed reversed (with the aid of a postscript printer driver)Text This printed text was folded and glued carefully to achieve a perfect transition in the wordsCylinder Still we have a problem beacuse if we take a photo with this setup and look at the center of the balls we can see the body of the rebelclose-up These are the kind of details that scores down our shots in this site. to fix this we can use this close-up to create a mask for our lens and put it at the top of the cylinder    With this trick we can hide our camera "completely".This is a shot without backlighting And this is the final shot with backlighting (the setup over a glass table) and without processing.  ', '2004-12-08 04:38:48.000000', NULL, 0),
