(1064578, 124383, 25486, '<td valign="top">Kylie, this is a cracking image!<br/> <br/>I didn''t vote in the challenge, though I did look through the entries, (quickly) and I remember seeing this one.  It stuck in my mind.  <br/> <br/>The contrasting colurs are great, the yellow on the orangy red of the wall, did you manipulate the colours much, at all?<br/> <br/>The shadows caused by the blinds are magnificent, they add depth and a feeling of being there, they somehow make it so real.<br/> <br/>The subject itself is quite interesting and that''s the key for me, take an interesting subject and add dramatic lighting, shoot from a interesting, original, different angle and you end up with something like this.  I know its not automated like that but that''s how I disect it.<br/> <br/>I just hope you remember me, and invite me to the opening night at your gallery!</td>', 'Kylie, this is a cracking image! I didn''t vote in the challenge, though I did look through the entries, (quickly) and I remember seeing this one.  It stuck in my mind.   The contrasting colurs are great, the yellow on the orangy red of the wall, did you manipulate the colours much, at all? The shadows caused by the blinds are magnificent, they add depth and a feeling of being there, they somehow make it so real. The subject itself is quite interesting and that''s the key for me, take an interesting subject and add dramatic lighting, shoot from a interesting, original, different angle and you end up with something like this.  I know its not automated like that but that''s how I disect it. I just hope you remember me, and invite me to the opening night at your gallery!', '2004-12-15 16:42:40.000000', NULL, 0),
